course: dictionary
lesson: 11824
title: Birthplace: where something begins
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A birthplace is the place where a person was born. It can be a town, a city or even a particular house. The word is made of two parts, birth and place, so you can work it out from those two words.
explain: «We visited the birthplace of William Shakespeare in Stratford-upon-Avon.» The clue is visited: people do not visit a place where they buy shoes, so it must be a special place connected to a famous person's start in life.
explain: A birthplace can also be where something started. «England is often called the birthplace of football.» Football was not born in a town. It means the place where football first began. Ask yourself: where did this start? That is usually the birthplace.
fact: A birthplace is the place where a person was born.
fact: Birthplace can also mean the place where something started or was first made or done.
fact: «Birthplace» is a noun, and its plural is «birthplaces».
fact: «Birthplace» is often used in phrases like the birthplace of jazz, the birthplace of football or the birthplace of democracy.
fact: On a form, «place of birth» asks where you were born, so it means the same as birthplace.
exercise: «Our class visited the birthplace of Shakespeare.» What is a birthplace? | *The place where a person was born | A kind of cake | A school for actors | A place where you buy birthday cards
exercise: «Jazz music began in New Orleans, the birthplace of jazz.» What does birthplace mean in this sentence? | A shop that sells instruments | *The place where jazz started | A party for music lovers | A school for singers
exercise: On a form, which question asks where you were born? | *Place of birth | Name of your best friend | Shoe size | Favourite colour
test: «Ella visited her birthplace, the town where she was born.» Which words explain what a birthplace is? | *the town where she was born | her birthplace | visited her | Ella visited
test: «England is often called the birthplace of football.» What does birthplace mean here? | *The place where football started | The place where the best players are sold | A place to play on Sundays | A football shop
exam: Where would you find the birthplace of jazz? | *In New Orleans, USA | On the moon | At the bottom of the sea | Inside a museum of cars
